  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Probiotics for sustainable Tilapia farming in East Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The biotechnology company NobleBio B.V. has been researching, developing and producing micro-organism cultures that can be a natural and sustainable alternative to chemicals used in the food, animal feed and aquaculture industries. NobleBio has specialised in the use of various &apos;good&apos; bacteria, probiotic strains, in the aquaculture sector as an alternative to antibiotics in fish feed and for water purification. This offers many benefits such as reducing antibiotic resistance, healthier fish with an increased weight and quantity, less chemical pollution of the water and a greater fish yield for fish farms.In Kenya, antibiotics are widely used in fish farms. This leads to resistance among bacteria and ultimately to lower yields and profitability for fish farmers. At the same time, the demand for fish consumption among the local population in Kenya is increasing. There are opportunities to set up more fish farms locally. However, this will have to be done in a more sustainable way with a different feed and water treatment. NobleBio sees opportunities to improve the sector with its knowledge and input. In this project, NobleBio initially focuses on treating the water and regulating the water quality around the fish, thereby reducing the toxins in the water.The demonstration project will take place at Lattice Aquaculture, a Kenyan aquaculture company that has two fish farms for demonstration and training purposes.</narrative>
  </description>
